;; The module _interpchannels (queue 230; Modules/_interpchannelsmodule.c of CPython 3.14.10): process-wide channels of
;; cross-interpreter data, under the GIL only. A channel has its queue, the interpreters bound to each end, and the
;; closing state: a send end closed while items remain leaves it "closing" until they are received. ChannelID is one
;; shared type (CPython's heap type per module); a closed channel's row stays in the table, as CPython's does while id
;; objects live (pyi's ids never report their death, so the row stays until destroy).

